      "output": "**Review record: Ice Fish Frenzy (static source review, not actually run)**\n\n**Method:** I read the HTML source only. The game was **not actually run**, so no item below is an execution result.\n\n**Defects found**\n1. **Startup crash (blocking).** `createPenguin` calls `new THREE.CapsuleGeometry(.42,.32,8,18)` for the body and `new THREE.CapsuleGeometry(.075,.24,4,8)` for the flippers. CapsuleGeometry first shipped in three.js r139, so it does not exist in r128. `HAT_COLORS.map(c=>{const p=createPenguin(c)…})` runs at top level, so it should throw \"not a constructor\". The render loop would then never start, and the canvas would stay blank. Fix: build the body from a cylinder plus spheres, or use `LatheGeometry`.\n2. **Start key and on-screen text disagree with the rules.** The rules say Enter. The code accepts `Space||Enter||NumpadEnter`, which is acceptable. However, the menu and results text say \"**Space** to start / play again\" and never mention Enter.\n3. **Minor: fish spawn on the menu.** The condition `if(st==='menu'||st==='play')` lets fish spawn while the menu is shown. `start()` calls `clearF()`, so the countdown starts clean. `menu()` does not clear leftover fish.\n\n**Confirmed by reading only**\n- **Key table:** `K[e.code]` is set on keydown and keyup, and `blur` clears it. Four `KS` sets are read every frame, and Numpad codes are separate from Digit codes.\n- **Player selection:** `Digit[234]` works on the menu only. Unused penguins are hidden and their scoreboards are set to opacity 0.3.\n- **Bouncing:** Collisions use 1/120 s substeps with overlap separation plus 1e-4. The impulse is applied only when `vn<0`, so penguins should not stick. Ghosting skips collision.\n- **Falling and respawn:** `hypot>FLOE_R` triggers the fall. After 2 s the penguin returns at (0,0) with a 1 s ghost period and no point loss.\n- **Fish:** Normal fish add +1 and golden fish +3. The cap is 6 live fish with at most 1 golden. The golden chance is 10%, spawns come every 0.8–1.4 s, and uncollected fish leave after 6 s.\n- **Timer:** The 60 s round starts after the 3 s countdown. Input is locked during the countdown, and the timer flashes at 10 s or less.\n- **Ranking and ties:** The rank formula is `1+count(higher)`, giving 1,1,3. Ties show \"Tie!\" and crown every tied leader.\n- **Play again:** `start()` resets `sc`, `win`, positions, fish and the contact state, and keeps N. Esc returns to the menu.\n- **Look in code:** Hats are mint, coral, yellow and sky blue with pom-poms. The scene has ice spray, splash, sparkles, icebergs, a flag, a buoy and gulls. Camera pitch is about 54.5°.\n- **External requests:** The only one is the cdnjs three.js r128 script.\n\n**Unverified (requires an actual run after fix 1)**\n- Real visual quality against the 3D-animated-short target.\n- Frame rate with 2048 shadows plus a 90×90 sea updated every frame.\n- Hardware key ghosting with four players on one keyboard.\n- Whether play actually feels good.\n- Audio.\n- Layout on different screen sizes."
